    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0312" n="1066" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1066"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/132</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-16T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>382. My telegrams 380 and 376 yesterday and November 14, respectively.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d201-f1"/> It is officially announced to-day that on the
                    initiative <pb facs="0313" n="1067" xml:id="pg1067"/> of the King of Sweden a
                    meeting of the three Scandinavian Kings accompanied by their Prime and Foreign
                    Ministers will be held in Christiania November 28 to 30, next. It is not
                    unreasonable to presume this meeting is in conformity with German wishes and is
                    being held for the purpose of keeping Norway in line with the policy of
                    Scandinavian cooperation. Such a course of action unquestionably has the support
                    of certain members of the Norwegian Government particularly the Foreign Minister
                    and the President of the Storthing.</p>
                <p>In view of the forthcoming meeting Department may consider it advisable that
                    conversations regarding Norwegian imports from America should be initiated here
                    at once in order that Norway may not after the meeting present us with a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">fait accompli</hi> if we delay beginning of
                    negotiations.</p>
                <p>British and French Ministers are telegraphing their Governments in the same
                    sense.</p>
                <p>Referring to the Department’s 180, November 14, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d201-f2"/> I am quite prepared to confer with McCormick at London
                    but will await further instructions before acting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
